# Klondike Solitaire
// Deal seven columns, then build four foundations, ace to king, one suit each:
// [wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Klondike_(solitaire)) has its rules, and what each pile is called.
// The cards, the deck and the piles are this project's own:  `Card`, `Deck` and `Pile`.

solitaire is an app:
	- its "score" is a number
	// What the card being dragged would add to the score, e.g. (+10):  shown beside it
	- its "hint" is text
	- its "deck" is a new deck

	// One of each, made with the solitaire
	- group "piles"
	- its "stock" is a new stock pile with name = "stock"
	- its "discards" is a new discard pile with name = "discards"
	- its "clubs" is a new foundation with name = "clubs", suit = clubs
	- its "diamonds" is a new foundation with name = "diamonds", suit = diamonds
	- its "hearts" is a new foundation with name = "hearts", suit = hearts
	- its "spades" is a new foundation with name = "spades", suit = spades
	- its "T1" is a new tableau with name = "T1"
	- its "T2" is a new tableau with name = "T2"
	- its "T3" is a new tableau with name = "T3"
	- its "T4" is a new tableau with name = "T4"
	- its "T5" is a new tableau with name = "T5"
	- its "T6" is a new tableau with name = "T6"
	- its "T7" is a new tableau with name = "T7"
	// Every card of its deck into the stock:  inside the loop `it` is the card, so the stock is the solitaire's
	- to create it:
		for each card in its deck
			add it to the stock of solitaire

	// Each pauses a moment, so a deal animates
	- group "dealing"
	// The discards, turned over, back into the stock
	- to reset the stock:
		set cards to a copy of list (its discards) as a pile
		reverse the cards
		for each card in the cards
			add it to the stock of the solitaire
			turn the card face down
	// turn the stock's next card over, onto the discards:  the discards back into the stock when it's empty
	- animation play from the stock:
		if its stock is empty
			wait for: reset the stock
		get the last card of its stock
		turn it face up
		pause for 50 msec
		add it to the discards of the solitaire
	// gather every card into the stock, shuffle it, and deal the tableaus:  one card more in each, left to right
	- animation deal the cards:
		for each card in its deck
			set start pile to the pile of the card
			turn the card face down
			if start pile is not the stock of the solitaire
				add the card to the stock of the solitaire
				pause for 50 msec
		shuffle its stock
		for row from 1 to 7
			turn the last card of its stock face up
			for column from row to 7
				add the last card of its stock to item column of the tableaus
				pause for 50 msec
		wait for: play from the stock


	// Its moves:  the menu's buttons, its keys, and the board's right click
	- group "game"
	- to start a new game:
		- shortcut N
		clear its score
		clear its hint
		deal the cards
	// Play every card that can go somewhere, until none can
	- to auto play:
		- shortcut A
		set anything changed to no
		if its discards is not empty
			set test card to the last card of its discards
			if await play test card
				set anything changed to yes
				pause for 500 msec
		// each tableau's last card onto its foundation
		for each pile in the tableaus
			if the pile is empty return
			set test card to the last card of the pile
			set foundation to the first pile in the foundations where its suit is the suit of test card
			if the foundation can take test card
				set anything changed to yes
				await play test card
				pause for 100 msec
		// each tableau's face-up cards, all together, onto another tableau
		for each pile in the tableaus
			set face up cards to the cards in the pile where the card is face up
			if face up cards is empty return
			set test card to the first card of face up cards
			if test card is a king and test card is the first card of the pile return
			if await play test card
				set anything changed to yes
				pause for 500 msec
		if anything changed await auto play
	// Turn up a face-down card from a tableau, at random, onto the discards
	- to cheat:
		- shortcut C
		set remaining piles to piles in the tableaus where it is not empty and its first card is face down
		if remaining piles is empty return
		set the pile to a random pile in remaining piles
		set the card to a random card in (the cards in the pile where the card is face down)
		turn the card face up
		pause for 30 ticks
		add the card to the discards of the solitaire
	- its "game menu" is a menu of "start a new game" , "-" , "auto play" and "cheat"

	// Its menu, then its piles seven to a line, the third cell empty;  a right click on the board shows the game menu
	- to draw it:
		<ui-container>
			<ui-menu>
				<ui-item kind="header">Klondike Solitaire</ui-item>
				<ui-item>Score: {its score}{its hint}</ui-item>
				<ui-menu position="right">
					<ui-item aria-label="Auto play" title="Auto play" onClick={auto play}><ui-icon name="fast forward"/></ui-item>
					<ui-item aria-label="Cheat" title="Cheat" onClick={cheat}><ui-icon name="eye"/></ui-item>
					<ui-item aria-label="Restart" title="Restart" onClick={start a new game}><ui-icon name="redo"/></ui-item>
				</ui-menu>
			</ui-menu>
			<ui-grid class="Board" columns="7" context-menu="game menu">
				{draw its stock}
				{draw its discards}
				<ui-column/>
				{draw its clubs}
				{draw its diamonds}
				{draw its hearts}
				{draw its spades}
				{draw its T1}
				{draw its T2}
				{draw its T3}
				{draw its T4}
				{draw its T5}
				{draw its T6}
				{draw its T7}
			</ui-grid>
		</ui-container>

## Playing a card
// What a click or a drag does:  the card's own moves, and each pile's, as the game plays them.

// the card, and every card on it, onto the first pile that takes it;  it says whether it moved
// - the stock's card turns over onto the discards instead
to play a card
	if the pile of the card is the stock of the solitaire
		play from the stock
		return
	set end pile to the first pile in every pile where it can take the card
	if there is not an end pile return no
	return put the card on end pile

// the card, and every card on it, onto the pile, if the piles' rules let it go and take it;  it says whether it moved
// - the pile it left turns its new last card up, and the move scores
to put a card on a pile
	set start pile to the pile of the card
	if start pile cannot give up the card return no
	if the pile cannot take the card return no
	set points to count the points for the card on the pile
	for each card in (cards in start pile starting with the card)
		move it to the pile
	if the start pile is a tableau and the start pile is not empty
		pause for 200 msec
		turn the last card of the start pile face up
	set the score of the solitaire to the score of the solitaire + points
	return yes

// what the move scores:  10 on a foundation, 5 from the discards, else nothing
to count the points for a card on a pile
	if the pile is a foundation return 10
	if the pile of the card is the discards of the solitaire return 5
	return 0

a pile:
	// while a card it would take is over it, the score shows what the move would add -- gone as the card leaves
	- while a card is dragged over it:
		set points to count the points for the card on it
		if it can take the card and points > 0: set the hint of the solitaire to " (+" + points + ")"
	- when a card is dropped on it:
		put the card on it

## The piles
// Each kind of pile, what it may take or give up, and how it lies.
// While one's empty, it shows its placeholder, if it has one.

// The cards not played yet, face down:  a click turns the next one over, so none can be taken from it
a "stock pile" is a pile:
	- its "layout" is stacked
	- it can never take a card
	- it can never let go of a card
	// A light grey card, face down:  a click turns the discards back over
	- to draw its placeholder:
		<ui-text part="placeholder" onClick={play from the stock}>🂠</ui-text>

// Where the stock's cards go as they're turned over
a "discard pile" is a pile:
	- its "layout" is stacked
	- it can never take a card
	- it can give up a card if: the card is its last card

// Where a suit is built up, ace to king, one card at a time
a "foundation" is a pile:
	- its "layout" is stacked
	- its "suit" is a card suit
	- it can never let go of a card
	- it can take a card if:
		if the card is not the last card of the pile of the card return no
		return its suit is the suit of the card and its value + 1 is the value of the card
	// A light grey ace of its suit, face up
	- to draw its placeholder:
		<ui-text part="placeholder">{the picture of a new card whose rank is ace and suit is its suit}</ui-text>

// A column, built down from king to ace, red and black in turn
a "tableau" is a pile:
	- its "layout" is vertical
	- it can give up a card if: the card is face up
	- it can take a card if:
		if it is empty
			return the card is a king
		return its color is not the color of the card and its value is the value of the card + 1

	- to test the moves:
		set the column to a new tableau with name = "T1"
		set the king to a new card whose rank is king, suit is spades and direction is up
		set the queen to a new card whose rank is queen, suit is hearts and direction is up
		set the jack to a new card whose rank is jack, suit is clubs and direction is up
		// an empty tableau takes only a king, then one lower in the other color
		the column can take the queen should be no
		the column can take the king should be yes
		add the king to the column
		the column can take the jack should be no
		the column can take the queen should be yes
		add the queen to the column
		the state of the column should be "T1: K♠↑ Q♥↑"
		the column can give up the queen should be yes
		turn the queen face down
		the column can give up the queen should be no

		// a foundation takes its suit, ace first, then one higher:  each the last card of its pile
		set the foundation to a new foundation with name = "hearts", suit = hearts
		set the two to a new card whose rank is 2, suit is hearts and direction is up
		set the ace to a new card whose rank is ace, suit is hearts and direction is up
		set the column to a new tableau with name = "T2"
		add the two to the column
		add the ace to the column
		the foundation can take the two should be no
		the foundation can take the ace should be yes
		move the ace to the foundation
		the foundation can take the two should be yes
		add the queen to the column
		the foundation can take the queen should be no

start a new game
start solitaire
